# GitHub Pages publishes EVERY tracked file on `main` verbatim (.nojekyll disables
# Jekyll, so `_config.yml`'s `exclude:` is inert). Anything committed here is served
# publicly at geesly.net/<path>. Untracking is the only way to keep a file off the site.

# Local-only working notes. Kept at the repo root because Claude Code auto-loads
# ./CLAUDE.md and would not find it in a subdirectory.
CLAUDE.md
.private/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Node (npm run dev pulls live-server via npx)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Full-resolution screenshot masters (1290x2796) for lib/images/N.webp.
# Untracked, not deleted: GitHub Pages serves every TRACKED file verbatim, so
# while these were committed they were live at geesly.net/lib/images/N.png —
# 11.2 MB that no page references and every crawler could fetch.
# They are not lost: recover any of them from history with
#   git show d930fa8:lib/images/1.png > lib/images/1.png
lib/images/1.png
lib/images/2.png
lib/images/3.png
lib/images/4.png
lib/images/5.png
lib/images/6.png

# Background artwork, unreferenced since the Organization logo moved to the
# square icon-512.png (Google wants a logo it can crop square; this was a
# 745 KB background). Untracked for the same reason as the masters above.
# Recover with: git show d930fa8:lib/images/geesly-background-no-text.png > lib/images/geesly-background-no-text.png
lib/images/geesly-background-no-text.png
